  "fields": {
    "title": "Digital Garden",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Digital gardens are personal, handwritten websites reminiscent of the first blogs of the 2000s, dedicated to a wide variety of topics and niches. They are often experimental, collage-like and artistic in their design, like early Myspace or Tumblr blogs, and deliberately not as predictable and uniform as current Instagram, Facebook or Twitter profiles. In most cases, the goal of such sites is not to generate feedback or enable social connections, but to create an own space, a place of relaxation, within the Internet – similar to a garden. Although the term ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "digital garden",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " or ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "digital gardening",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " has existed since the end of the 90s, it has experienced a new upswing in recent years. ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6gs1oeKWJBrcjrN8eEPPl8",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Background",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "In 1998, Mark Bernstein introduced the idea of the ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "uri": "http://www.eastgate.com/garden/Enter.html"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ],
                  "value": "hypertext garden",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ", in which he argued for spaces on the Internet where one can immerse oneself in the unknown.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ],
                  "value": "»Gardens (...) lie between farmland and wilderness. The garden is farmland that delights the senses, designed for delight rather than commodity.« ",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                },
                {
                  "data": {
                    "target": {
                      "sys": {
                        "id": "6jYmBv1BSm28PbJRDXgqa0",
                        "type": "Link",
                        "linkType": "Entry"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "superscript"
                        }
                      ],
                      "value": "[2]",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                },
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": " ",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
